            "text": "<p>Quercetin is a flavanoid found naturally in a number of foods including apples, onions, teas, berries, and red wine. Quercetin has been shown to encourage a healthy immune response, especially to seasonally changing environments. Quercitin acts as an antioxidant, neutralizing free radicals—the chemical by-products that harm cell membranes and damage DNA. Quercetin possesses significant antihistamine and anti-inflammatory properties. Quercetin's best-known mechanism of action involves its ability to stabilize mast cell membranes, which in turn can decrease the release of histamine. In this way it provides nutritional support for individuals who occasionally suffer from allergies. This bioflavonoid also supports healthy cholesterol levels already within normal range.<br/><br/>For more information of Hi-Tech's proprietary Cyclosome Technology - visit<br/><a href=\"http://cyclosometechnology.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://cyclosometechnology.com/</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "product_item_XUPcgw": {
          "type": "product_item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/download_20.avif",
            "image_alt": "",
            "link": "https://hitechpharma.com/collections/healthcare/products/shilajit-extract",
            "title": "SHILAJIT EXTRACT",
            "text": "<p>Shilajit is one of the fastest growing supplements available. It is a monstrously diverse pitch that grows on surfaces of granite rocks in several regions of the world. This pitch contains a who’s-who of the mineral spectrum and functionality factor. Shilajit has been used in traditional Indian Ayurvedic medicine for centuries, and the compounds in it appear to be beneficial for many conditions. Found only in high altitude rock formations, this sticky tar like substance is a byproduct of plant degradation in the wild. Research notes that two of the key compounds in Shilajit – Fulvic and Humic Acids, act both as antioxidant and anti-inflammatory compounds and may help reduce cell wall damage and reduce free-radical formation in the body. These are the primary two key factors in immune health and the overall ageing process.<br/><br/>For more information of Hi-Tech's proprietary Cyclosome Technology - visit<br/><a href=\"http://cyclosometechnology.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://cyclosometechnology.com/</a></p>"
          }
        },
